.===============================================================================
.TITLE{The question}

.center
.css{font-size: 6svh; margin-top: 5svh;}
Go has no official project structure.
.css.end
.center.end

.center
.css{font-size: 8svh; margin-top: 3svh; color: #AA0000;}
**So… what do I do?**
.css.end
.center.end

.notes
Relate to the audience: everyone has asked "where do I put this file?" in Go.
Go's lack of a prescribed structure is intentional - it's about choosing what fits YOUR project.
.notes.end

.===============================================================================
.TITLE{What we'll cover}

- 8 layout approaches using same example app
- From flat structure to hexagonal architecture
- Popular layouts from 2014 to today (2026)
- **My** take on prominent common Go project layouts
- In the wild there are mixes
- Some I did not encounter for sure
- If you have favorit layout I did not list, show us!
